# Game design context

Read `docs/GAME_DESIGN.md` before making gameplay or balance changes.

- **North star:** **Loop Road with two boards** — (1) circular **walk map** (right) where the player advances and hits enemy stations; (2) **5×5 chain board** always visible on the left. Pack before engage; board locks in combat; rearrange only outside the battlefield.
- **Combat:** Attack auto-loops until KO. Opening bombs placed once at Engage; they tick after each card round and persist. No mid-fight enemy board placement.
- **Flow:** Home → walk map + prep board → Engage station (lock + place bombs) → Attack (auto-loop) → unlock → map → loot → home. Optional dungeon.
- **Entry point:** `App.tsx` → loop hub / `LoopMapOverlay` + Phaser via `START_BATTLE` (`loopPrep`) / `LOOP_ENGAGE` / `LOOP_RESUME_PREP` / `LOOP_FINISH`.
- **Determinism:** seed-based RNG in `src/game/random/rng.ts` — never `Math.random()` in gameplay.
- **Removed:** TD code. Do not recreate it.
- **When changing systems:** Update `docs/GAME_DESIGN.md` changelog and roadmap.
